name": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Nilesh: 15, Yash: 15, Akshay: 5, Nikhil: 10, Srijan: 10", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:40:07Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "next", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:40:16Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "4.\tThe Greek word X means a flat circular plate — originally referring to the heavy stone or metal object thrown in athletic competitions in the ancient Olympics, immortalized in Myron's famous statue. Latin borrowed it, and from Latin, English borrowed it four separate times, ending up with four very different objects. The earliest borrowing predates the Norman Conquest by centuries. It entered Old English directly, when the Latin “sk” sound was already shifting to “sh” in some Germanic dialects. This gives us Y, a flat piece of crockery. The second borrowing Z came through Old French and refers to a raised platform — originally the high table in a medieval hall, where the lord of the manor and his honored guests sat. The third borrowing came through Medieval Latin possibly via Italian, and gives us A — a piece of furniture that all of us use everyday. The fourth and most recent borrowing came directly from Latin in the 17th century, and gives us B, used today for everything from records to frisbees to the round things in your spine with different spelling variants in Britain and America. ID X (5 points), Y (5 points), Z (5 points), A (5 points), and B (5 points). For X, I will accept either the Greek or Latin word.", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:40:29Z", "username": "Nilesh", "text": "discus", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:40:31Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "Dish", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:40:38Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "Disc", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:40:39Z", "username": "Yash Agrawal", "text": "desk", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:40:53Z", "username": "Yash Agrawal", "text": "dais", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:41:04Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Answers: X=diskos (discus in Latin), Y=dish, Z=dais, A=desk, B=disc/disk", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:41:48Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Nilesh: 20, Yash: 25, Akshay: 5, Nikhil: 10, Srijan: 20", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-29T14:41:59Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "next", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]